# A shim, and it must stay one. Git needs a file it can execute; everything it
# does is Node, because Node behaves the same on Linux, macOS and Windows and a
# shell does not (CLAUDE.md → Three systems). Do not grow logic in here —
# scripts/pre-commit.test.ts fails when it appears.
exec node scripts/dev/pre-commit.mjs
